0..73 Comment "// A case on a vector: a case that writes every constructor of an indexed"
74..147 Comment "// family checks each arm at its own constructor\'s fields, as a case on a"
148..209 Comment "// family with no indices does (Dybjer, _Inductive families_,"
210..282 Comment "// doi:10.1007/BF01211308). An arm whose constructor cannot stand at the"
283..359 Comment "// scrutinee\'s index is still written; leaving it out is in the pathological"
360..368 Comment "// twin."
370..407 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
